The "back-up of saved game cheat" has been discussed before and works on
several computers (I own an Atari ST).  You can also collect bone-files
this way.  Don't you hate starving to death just when you got a +20 long
sword, all instrinsics and the rest? Drop everything if you're sure
you're going to die to avoid cursed status and you really have something
to look out for (but you don't always get a bones file).  Keep a backup
copy for future games if you do.

Another cheat that works on the Atari (btw.  I play version 3.0j) is to
set the option that you're going to use a RAMdisk in the nethack.cnf
file.  Do not create said RAMdisk when you restore a saved file. 
Nethack will not be able to create the levels on the RAMdisk and will
quit, asking you whether you want to see what you were carrying, what
your intrinsics are etc.  You are even added to the scorefile, BUT the
saved game is NOT erased! So, free identification of all objects.  I
guess this also works on PC and Mac.  It should be easy to eliminate
this 'bug'. 

Personally I find that cheating helps to win, but it doesn't give any
real satisfaction or joy.  The game is not about winning, it's about
having fun. But if other people have fun cheating, let them.

